**Code Explanation:**

The code performs the initial data pre-processing and CMB filtering required to isolate the sub-dominant kSZ signal. First, it loads the observed map, the ground-truth maps (CMB, kSZ, noise), and the halo catalog. It computes and prints the root-mean-square (RMS) of each map to establish the baseline variance of the different components. To construct the Wiener filter, the code defines a 2D Fourier space grid of multipoles (ell) based on the map's physical dimensions (10x10 degrees, 1200x1200 pixels). The analytical LambdaCDM temperature power spectrum D_ell is computed and converted to C_ell^CMB. This theoretical spectrum is then multiplied by the beam transfer function squared (B_ell^2) to account for the 1.4 arcmin FWHM Gaussian beam convolution present in the observed map. The noise power spectrum is defined analytically as white noise (C_ell^noise = sigma^2 * Omega_pix), while the kSZ power spectrum is computed empirically from the ground-truth kSZ map. The Wiener filter is constructed as W(ell) = C_ell^CMB / (C_ell^CMB + C_ell^noise + P_ksz). This filter represents the optimal linear estimator for the primary CMB. The filter is applied to the observed map in Fourier space, and the resulting estimated CMB map is subtracted from the observed map to produce the cleaned_map. A perfect cleaned map is also generated by subtracting the ground-truth CMB map, which will serve as a theoretical benchmark in later steps. Finally, the code computes the 1D radially averaged power spectra for all components and the Wiener filter transfer function. These are plotted on a log-log scale to visually diagnose the filtering process, showing how the filter suppresses the CMB at scales where it dominates and drops to zero at high multipoles where noise takes over. The cleaned maps, the filter, the beam transfer function, and the diagnostic plot are saved to the data/ directory. The function get_1d_ps(P2d, ell2d, pixel_size_rad, bins=100) computes the 1D radially averaged power spectrum up to the Nyquist frequency.

**Modifications:**

Modified get_1d_ps to limit the maximum ell bin to the Nyquist frequency, eliminating the high-ell staircase artifacts caused by the corners of the 2D FFT grid. Changed the right y-axis (for the Wiener filter) to a logarithmic scale and set a lower limit of 1e-6 to better visualize the filter's behavior at high multipoles. Simplified the legend labels and repositioned them to avoid overlapping with the data lines.

